## Cross-System Relationships (Logical)

| From | Field | To | Nature |
|---|---|---|---|
| SafeSight Patient | homeUserId | MedicalUser._id | Many-to-one (home patient linked to user account) |
| SafeSight VitalLog | patientId | Patient._id | Many-to-one (each log belongs to one patient) |
| SafeSight MedicalAlert | patientId | Patient._id | Many-to-one |
| SafeSight LabReport | patientId | Patient._id | Many-to-one |
| MedFlow2 VitalLog | patientId | MedFlow2 Patient.bedId | Many-to-one |
| MedFlow2 Alert | patientId / bedId | MedFlow2 Patient.bedId | Many-to-one |
| MedFlow2 Task | bedId | MedFlow2 Patient.bedId | Many-to-one |
| MedFlow2 PoseFrame | bedId | MedFlow2 Patient.bedId | Many-to-one |
| EcoTrack WasteLog | vehicleId | Vehicle.vehicleId | Many-to-one |
| EcoTrack WasteLog | binId | Bin.binId | Many-to-one |
| EcoTrack WasteLog | driverId | User._id (driver role) | Many-to-one |
| EcoTrack Route | vehicleId | Vehicle.vehicleId | Many-to-one |
| EcoTrack Route | driverId | User._id | Many-to-one |
| EcoTrack Route waypoints | binId | Bin.binId | Many-to-many (embedded) |
| EcoTrack Schedule | vehicleId | Vehicle.vehicleId | Many-to-one |
| EcoTrack Alert | vehicleId | Vehicle.vehicleId | Many-to-one |
| EcoTrack Alert | binId | Bin.binId | Many-to-one |
| SmartRetail Footfall | zoneId | Camera.zone | Many-to-one |
| SmartRetail Alert | zone | Camera.zone | Many-to-one (logical) |

---

## AI Engine (Python / No DB)
The **AI Engine** (`ai-engine/src/detection.py`) is a Python service using:
- **YOLOv8** for object detection (persons, fall detection)
- **YOLOv8-Pose** for pose estimation (17-keypoint skeleton)
- **OpenCV** for video/frame processing
- **FastAPI** (Port 4000) serving REST endpoints
- It **does not have its own database** — it pushes results (alerts, pose frames) to the **SafeSight Web Dashboard** via REST API calls authenticated with API keys from the `apikeys` collection.

---

## Instructions for the diagram

1. Use **Mermaid `erDiagram`** syntax.
2. Group entities with comment headers for each sub-system.
3. Show **all fields** from the tables above.
4. Use these Mermaid types: `string`, `number`, `boolean`, `date`, `objectId`, `mixed`, `array`.
5. Mark PKs with `PK` and FKs with `FK` in attribute comments.
6. Show **all relationships** from the Cross-System table above with proper cardinality (one-to-many, many-to-one etc.).
7. Add a note/legend explaining the 4 sub-systems and the AI Engine's role.
8. Make the diagram thesis-quality, clean, and well-organized.
